local-first-ai-agent 0.1.0
Application source: https://github.com/gimesha-adikari/local-first-ai-agent
Copyright: local-first-ai-agent contributors
Application license: Apache-2.0. The full license is included below.

The shipped LFM2.5 model carries the LFM Open License v1.0. Its full license
and model notice are installed with the model in
/usr/lib/local-first-ai-agent/models/. The source copies are in
third_party/model-licenses/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct. Model files have separate terms.

Third-party source availability
-------------------------------
option-ext 0.2.0 is covered by the Mozilla Public License 2.0. Its exact,
unmodified registry source archive is included at
/usr/share/doc/local-first-ai-agent/sources/option-ext-0.2.0.crate and is
also available without charge from
https://static.crates.io/crates/option-ext/option-ext-0.2.0.crate
SHA-256: 04744f49eae99ab78e0d5c0b603ab218f515ea8cfe5a456d7629ad883a3b6e7d
The archive contains the MPL-2.0 text and source code. The license is also
reproduced below. Other component source links are recorded by version.

Rust standard library 1.100.0
----------------------------
The toolchain's library-specific license and copyright report is included
as rust-COPYRIGHT-library.html in this directory. The corresponding source
tree is https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/tree/1.100.0/library.

System integration
------------------
The executable uses distribution-provided shared libraries including GTK 3,
GDK, GdkPixbuf, GLib/GIO, Cairo, WebKitGTK, JavaScriptCoreGTK, libsoup, D-Bus,
glibc, libstdc++ and libgcc. Several include LGPL-covered code. They are
loaded through the standard Linux shared-library mechanism. The app can
be used with ABI-compatible replacements. The package also invokes the
system Poppler, Bubblewrap and util-linux utilities for isolated PDF reading.
The distribution supplies those packages separately, with component terms
in their own /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright files and corresponding
source packages. GNU Library/Lesser GPL 2 and 2.1 texts are included below.

Software component index
------------------------
This documents the pinned Linux normal application dependency graph
(excluding procedural macros), locked npm production closure plus
Tailwind, Vite and Rolldown output contributors, and reviewed native and
toolchain notices.
Dependency closures may include code eliminated by the link or frontend
bundler. Identical legal texts are listed once and referenced by number.

